    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Criteria for the diagnosis of lung neuroendocrine tumours</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Nicholson AG",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Typical carcinoid</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A tumour &ge; 5 mm with carcinoid morphology and &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>, lacking necrosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Atypical carcinoid</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A tumour with carcinoid morphology and 2&ndash;10&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> and/or necrosis (often punctate) or both</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A tumour with neuroendocrine morphology (organoid nesting, palisading, rosettes, trabeculae)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>High mitotic count: &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>, median of 70&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Necrosis (often in large zones)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Cytological features of a non-small cell carcinoma, as well as large cell size; low N:C&nbsp;ratio; vesicular, coarse, or fine chromatin; and/or frequent nucleoli; some tumours have fine nuclear chromatin and lack nucleoli but qualify as non-small cell carcinoma because of large cell size and abundant cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Positive immunohistochemical staining for one or more neuroendocrine markers (other than NSE) and/or neuroendocrine granules by electron microscopy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Small cell lung carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 678.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Small size (generally less than the diameter of 3&nbsp;small resting lymphocytes)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Scant cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Nuclei: finely granular nuclear chromatin, absent or faint nucleoli</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>High mitotic count: &gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>, median of 80&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Frequent necrosis (often in large zones)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]